sequenceDiagram
    %% Auth flow 4 of 4 — Sign out
    %% Participants map to:
    %%   PR   src/screens/ProfileScreen.js
    %%   AU   src/services/auth.js
    %%   AS   src/stores/authStore.js
    %%   ES   src/utils/enhancedStorage.js
    %%   RPS  src/stores/readingProgressStore.js
    %%   CS   src/stores/commentsStore.js
    %%   OS   roomStore, bucketsStore, booksStore, notificationStore
    %%   NAV  src/navigation/AppNavigator.js
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant PR as ProfileScreen
    participant AU as auth.js
    participant SRV as Server
    participant AS as authStore
    participant ES as enhancedStorage
    participant RPS as readingProgressStore
    participant CS as commentsStore
    participant OS as Other stores
    participant NAV as AppContent

    U->>PR: "Sign Out"
    PR->>ES: getRefreshToken() (read at render)
    PR->>SRV: unregisterPushDevice() → DELETE /users/me/devices/{fcm token}
    Note over PR: First, while the access token is still<br/>stored. Best effort — the server also moves<br/>a token to whoever registers it next
    PR->>AU: logout(username, refreshToken)
    AU->>SRV: POST /auth/logout?username=…, Bearer refreshToken {skipAuthRetry}
    SRV-->>AU: status (logged, not checked)
    PR->>AS: signOut()
    AS->>AS: user, tokens = null, isAuthenticated = false
    AS->>ES: clearAuthData() — token, profile, refresh token
    AS->>RPS: clearProgress() — in-memory only
    AS->>CS: clearComments()
    AS->>OS: clearRooms() (+ roomsLoaded = false), clearBuckets(),<br/>clearBooks(), clearNotifications()
    Note over ES: Reading positions and preferences stay<br/>in MMKV, scoped by username, so the same<br/>reader gets them back on next sign-in
    AS-->>NAV: isAuthenticated false
    NAV->>NAV: unmount Main, mount Auth → Login
    Note over AS: The same signOut runs when a refresh<br/>token is rejected (auth-03), so a forced<br/>sign-out clears exactly as much
